WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:07.018
Welcome to AI Literacy. In this lesson, you will learn what artificial intelligence is, and what it is not.

00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:13.458
Artificial intelligence is software that learns patterns from huge numbers of examples.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:20.237
It then makes a best guess: the next word, what is in a photo, or an answer to a question.

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:26.366
You already use AI for voice typing, translation and face unlock on your phone.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.498
AI predicts likely answers, so it can sound sure of itself and still be wrong.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:37.359
It may know little about Liberia or your community, because it saw few examples.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.617
So treat AI as a fast assistant, and always check its work.

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:53.536
Before you move on, check: Name three AI tools you already use. Say one thing AI is good at. Say why AI answers must be checked.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.475
In the next lesson: Talking to AI assistants.
